    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe \"[Process exited N]\" / \"[Terminal closed]\" virtual text has no highlight group. So it can't be dimmed with `nvim_set_hl`. The only way today is a `TermClose` autocmd that waits with `vim.schedule`, reads the extmarks in the `nvim.terminal.exitmsg` namespace, and sets each one again with a highlight group.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nGive the message a highlight group, so it can be changed with one line, e.g.:\n\n    vim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, \"TermExitMsg\", { link = \"NonText\" })",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-31T13:29:41Z",
    "closed_by": {
