            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I'm not really sure we want to build a lot of chrome around this message.\n\n> The only way today is a `TermClose` autocmd that waits with `vim.schedule`, reads the extmarks in the `nvim.terminal.exitmsg` namespace, and sets each one again with a highlight group.\n\nYou can instead just clear the namespace/message, and handle `TermClose` + `v:event.status` however you want. That's a bit simpler? Also note that `nvim_get_chan_info().exitcode` is available.",
            "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:29:41Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42603#issuecomment-6543994274",
            "id": 6543994274,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/42603",
